  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Disaster Risk Management (DRM) and Climate Change Adaptation Capacity in Libya - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to the Notre Dame Global Adaptation Index, Libya is among one of the least prepared countries to face the challenges of climate change. In recent years, some regions in Libya have been repeatedly affected by extreme weather conditions, often in insecure and institutionally vulnerable environments, heightening the risk of intensifying disputes over scarce resources and undermining social cohesion. Building on the ongoing Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance Disaster Risk Management (DRM) activities, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) in Libya is further contributing to strengthening the resilience of communities affected by, or at risk of being affected by hazards, and consequently reinforcing national response capacity (through structured local investments) to mitigate the impact of climate-related disasters in Libya.</narrative>
  </description>
